On 10/04/2024, 11:49=E2=80=AFPM, "Brent Molyneux KC" <BMolyneux@29br.co.uk> wrote=
:

=20

=20

Hi Nadia

=20

The judgment represents the judge=E2=80=99s analysis of the evidence and the deci=
sion based upon it. If you disagree with his analysis and decision then you =
can try and appeal it (but do not read this as being advice that you should =
appeal).

 I don=E2=80=99t understand your reference to my duties in this context.

I think you need to apply for a transcript (it=E2=80=99s expensive). I don=E2=80=99t kn=
ow what the process is -

the court should be able to help.

I wish to (and intend to) lodge a list of typographical amendments. I am no=
t intending to seek your approval as this is a purely administrative exercis=
e to help the court. If you object to that, you will have to contact the jud=
ge and explain why, and the judge will then be able to make a decision as to=
 whether any typographical corrections require your agreement and input.

Best wishes

Brent=20

=20

